#Htrow-prep.lic
#Two-handed-weapon Sorcerer version of Brayis-prep.lic (Htrowelzzif). No Magic
#Item Use, so no gold coin and no wands -- gearing up is clearing hands,
#rubbing the five items that work without it, and READY 2WEAP.

module HtrowPrep

# clear hands -- "store 2weap" puts the two-hander (a scorched invar flail as of
# 11/08) back in the hooded cloak per her STORE 2weapon setting; "stow all"
# mops up anything else left in a hand.
fput "store 2weap"
fput "stow all"

# rub stuff, but only if the spell isn't already active -- and only pause
# after ones that actually ran, instead of always eating 3s per item. The cube
# and orb crumble after one rub; Htrow-prerest restocks all five.
unless Spell[1712].active?   # Spirit Guard
  Script.run("qverb", "rub small statue")
  pause 3
end
unless Spell[1705].active?   # Martial Prowess
  Script.run("qverb", "rub moonstone cube")
  pause 3
end
unless Spell[1711].active?   # Mystic Focus
  Script.run("qverb", "rub quartz orb")
  pause 3
end
unless Spell[509].active?    # Strength
  Script.run("qverb", "rub white crystal")
  pause 3
end
unless Array(GameObj.loot).find { |i| i.name =~ /#{Char.name} disk/ }
  Script.run("qverb", "rub black crystal")
  pause 3
end

# two-hander to the right hand
fput "ready 2weap"

# No weapon in the right hand: it's really gone (disarmed and never recovered,
# or the STORE 2weapon setting points at something that isn't there). Don't let
# bigshot walk back out bare-handed -- stop it here, in town, the same way
# Brayis-prep.lic does. This runs before any travel (bigshot's
# hunting_prep_commands happen at the start of pre_hunt). Right hand only: GS4
# holds a two-hander there, and the attack script checks the same hand.
pause 0.5
if checkright.nil?
  echo "Htrow-prep: no weapon in the right hand after READY 2WEAP -- stopping bigshot. " \
       "Check the STORE 2weapon setting (STORE LIST)."
  Script.kill("bigshot") if Script.running?("bigshot")
  exit
end

# Puts away loot eloot has no room for and unpauses it, so a full cloak can't
# leave you fighting with your hands full (see eloot_guard.lic).
Script.start("eloot_guard") unless Script.running?("eloot_guard")

end #End of module
